# TypeScript conventions

Edit-time checklist for all `.ts` / `.tsx` in the monorepo. Canonical detail: [STYLE.md](../docs/contributors/STYLE.md) § TypeScript, [STYLEGUIDE.md](../docs/contributors/STYLEGUIDE.md). Baseline: [tsconfig.base.json](../tsconfig.base.json) (`strict`, `isolatedModules`).

**Precedence:** Under `packages/ui/src/components/**`, this rule covers **TypeScript only**. CVA, token prefix, layer exports → [ui-components.mdc](./ui-components.mdc). JSDoc → [code-commenting.mdc](./code-commenting.mdc).

---

## Do not

- Use `any` (explicit or implicit).
- Use `catch (error)` without typing — use `catch (error: unknown)` and narrow before use.
- Value-import type-only symbols (`import { Foo }` when `Foo` is type-only).
- Use `export function` — use `export const` arrow functions.
- Use TypeScript `enum` — use string literal unions and `as const` tuples.
- Use non-null assertion `!`.
- Deep-import another package's `src/` or internal `dist/` — public API via `package.json` `exports` only ([AGENTS.md](../AGENTS.md)).

---

## Import style

- Use `import type` or inline `import { value, type Type }` for type-only symbols.
- Prefer one import line per module (avoid duplicate lines from the same path).
- ESM only — no `require()`.
- In `packages/cli` and `packages/registry`, use `node:` for Node.js built-ins (`node:fs/promises`, `node:path`, …).

---

## Module resolution

| Package area | Relative imports |
| ------------ | ---------------- |
| `packages/ui`, `packages/tokens` | Bundler — no `.js` extension on relatives |
| `packages/cli`, `packages/registry` | NodeNext — **`.js`** extension on all relative imports |

Cross-package imports use published package names only — never `@scope/package/src/...`.

---

## Errors and boundaries

- Narrow `unknown` at JSON parse, config read, and CLI arg boundaries — not `as any`.
- Prefer `// @ts-expect-error` over `// @ts-ignore`; if used, one-line reason.
- CLI user-facing failures: `CliError` with recovery hint; let `handleCliError` be the exit path (see STYLE / `packages/cli`).

---

## Types and exports

| Use `interface` | Use `type` |
| --------------- | ---------- |
| Extendable object props, component props | Unions, mapped types, generic aliases |

- Annotate return types on **exported** functions; internal helpers may infer.
- UI components may infer JSX return type; still use `export const`, `displayName`, and a single `export { … }` block at file bottom (STYLE § React Components).
- Use `satisfies` only for const objects/literals where literal inference must be preserved (registry items, preset ids) — not for parameters or simple strings. See STYLE.

```typescript
// Bad — missing .js on relative import in cli/registry
import { loadConfig } from "../config/config"
```

---

## Type assertions

- Prefer type guards over assertions.
- When asserting, cast through `unknown` — not across unrelated types.
- No `!` operator — explicit checks or guards.

---

## Naming

File, export, and symbol casing: [STYLE.md](../docs/contributors/STYLE.md) § Naming only — no duplicate tables here.

---

## `readonly`

Use `readonly` on schema/config arrays in tokens and registry where mutation would be a bug. UI prop interfaces do not require `readonly`.

